  note    `Allow` lists every method a route of the path takes, sorted, `HEAD` where `GET` is, and `OPTIONS`, which `not_routed` answers: `DELETE, GET, HEAD, OPTIONS` where Go writes `DELETE, GET, HEAD` (observed)

capability route/options  OPTIONS answered with the methods allowed
  heroes  web.not_routed
  go      echo's automatic OPTIONS answer
  rust    -
  python  werkzeug.routing.Map's provide_automatic_options, flask.Flask.make_default_options_response
  note    204 and `Allow`, as Echo and Flask answer, where Go answers 405 (observed); a route of `OPTIONS` takes it first

capability route/head  HEAD taken by the route of GET
  heroes  web.route
  go      net/http.ServeMux's GET pattern answering HEAD (observed), chi/middleware.GetHead
  rust    -
