capability serve/stateful  the loop a program with state writes: accept, read, route, call its own function with its `@` state, write
  heroes  http.next_request, http.write_answer, web.route, web.not_routed
  go      echo.Context.Set, echo.Context.Get, gin.Context.Set, Get, MustGet, chi/middleware.WithValue, a closure over the program's state
  rust    -
  python  flask.g, flask.current_app, flask.Flask.app_context
  note    no closure carries the state: the router answers the route's name and the program calls its own function with its `@` state, in the loop of `route`'s example; `http.next_request` answers 100, 400, 413, 417, 431, 501 and 505 and `http.write_answer` keeps an HTTP/1.0 connection alive, as `http.serve` does

